== Normalized definitions ==

=== Information ===
Information is a broad concept concerning distinctions, uncertainty reduction, representation, communication, or content, with discipline-specific meanings.

=== Information theory ===
Information theory is the mathematical study of quantifying, coding, transmitting, and processing information under uncertainty and noise.

=== Entropy ===
Entropy is a family of quantitative concepts measuring multiplicity, uncertainty, or dispersal under specified mathematical or physical formalisms.

=== Feedback ===
Feedback occurs when information about a system's output or state returns into the system and influences subsequent behavior.

=== Emergence ===
Emergence describes higher-level patterns, properties, or behaviors arising from interactions among lower-level components.

=== Self-organization ===
Self-organization is the formation or maintenance of organized macroscopic pattern through local interactions/internal dynamics without a central controller specifying the global pattern.

=== Complex system ===
A complex system is a system whose collective behavior depends strongly on interactions among components and often exhibits nonlinear, multiscale, adaptive, or emergent dynamics.

=== Network ===
A network is a set of entities connected by relationships or interactions, often represented mathematically by a graph.

=== Robustness ===
Robustness is the ability of a system/model/process to maintain specified function or structure under perturbation, uncertainty, faults, or variation.

=== Adaptation (systems) ===
Systems adaptation is change in state, structure, policy, organization, or behavior in response to conditions such that persistence, fit, or performance is maintained or improved relative to some criterion.

== Required non-equivalences ==

<pre>
information ≠ data
information ≠ meaning by definition
information theory ≠ semantics
entropy ≠ disorder by definition
Shannon entropy ≠ thermodynamic entropy by identity
feedback ≠ ordinary-language response
negative feedback ≠ harmful feedback
positive feedback ≠ beneficial feedback
emergence ≠ self-organization
emergence ≠ mystery
self-organization ≠ absence of external influence
complex system ≠ merely complicated system
network ≠ computer network
network ≠ graph by strict identity
robustness ≠ resilience
robustness ≠ reliability
adaptation ≠ robustness
adaptation ≠ evolution by definition
</pre>

== Source roles ==

* Shannon; Cover & Thomas; MacKay — information theory.
* SEP Information — senses of information and Shannon/thermodynamic distinction.
* statistical mechanics texts — thermodynamic/statistical entropy.
* Wiener; MIT feedback/control literature — feedback.
* Mitchell; Holland; Santa Fe Institute — complex/adaptive systems, emergence, self-organization.
* Newman; Barabási; network-science literature — network structure/dynamics.
* Nature Reviews Physics 2024 — robustness/resilience of complex networks.

